1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,680
[This series contains scenes of violence,
self-harm, and potential triggers.]

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:05,150
Damn it, I'm late! I'm doomed!

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,310
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:08,260
Humanity is waiting for me!

5
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:10,640
Just let humanity keep waiting.

6
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,770
I can't. Today's humanity

7
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,510
will be giving me money.

8
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:19,160
Ugh, who is it?

9
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:21,620
Hello?

10
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:23,850
It's you, the wicked songwriter.

11
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:25,950
What? The document envelope?

12
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,850
Uh-huh. Yes, I have it.

13
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,390
Bring it to you?

14
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:32,910
I can't! I'm busy—

15
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,460
Damn it.

16
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:39,360
My dear protégé.

17
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:43,930
Get up. This is also
part of the training, kiddo.

18
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:45,050
I don't want to!

19
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:46,830
To build your stamina.

20
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:49,150
Put on your shoes and deliver it now!

21
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,470
Go quickly.

22
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:51,950
Hurry up!

23
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,940
I'm putting on my shoes.

24
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:53,790
Put them on as you go!

25
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:54,790
Get going now.

26
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:56,050
Hurry up!

27
00:00:56,170 --> 00:00:57,260
Go!

28
00:00:57,410 --> 00:00:58,600
Damn it.

29
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,850
Hanyul.

30
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:29,920
I missed you so much, Lee Hanyul.

31
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:37,030
Where on earth have you been hiding?

32
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:39,700
It took me forever to find you.

33
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:47,940
Wake up. Don't play dead.

34
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:49,910
Hey, is he really dead?

35
00:01:50,039 --> 00:01:51,380
Murderer.

36
00:01:53,009 --> 00:01:55,460
Is this how you talk to a friend, Hanyul?

37
00:01:56,390 --> 00:01:59,910
Don't you remember how much I liked you?

38
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:02,380
You liked me too,

39
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,840
didn't you?

40
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:05,720
No,

41
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:07,240
I didn't.

42
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,160
Hanyul.

43
00:02:13,150 --> 00:02:14,680
He said he doesn't like you.

44
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:21,190
You have no business
getting involved in this.

45
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,560
This is the hallway of my office.

46
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,060
This is between Hanyul and me.

47
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,840
Then it's half my business too.

48
00:02:40,579 --> 00:02:42,720
I'll just pretend you're dead too.

49
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:45,400
Don't ever show up in front of me again.

50
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,220
Looks like we're starting over,

51
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,440
Hanyul.

52
00:03:03,310 --> 00:03:10,140
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

53
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:16,010
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

54
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,760
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

55
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:21,690
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

56
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:39,770
[Yoo Dohyun]

57
00:03:39,890 --> 00:03:41,380
[Cho Chanhyeon]

58
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,050
[Ko Gyeol]

59
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:48,020
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

60
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:53,070
Didn't you come to bring me that?

61
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:57,860
You know Herod?

62
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,390
Why didn't you tell me?

63
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:02,540
It's nothing. He's just
an artist under our agency.

64
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:06,310
Wait... Are you two conspiring against me?

65
00:04:06,810 --> 00:04:10,340
Couldn't you tell from the atmosphere
just now? Obviously not.

66
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:11,630
That aside,

67
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,050
were you in love with Herod?

68
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,410
He said you used to like him—

69
00:04:16,410 --> 00:04:17,630
I wasn't.

70
00:04:19,019 --> 00:04:20,310
Right?

71
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,050
He's so ugly.

72
00:04:22,490 --> 00:04:24,600
He should at least be of my caliber.

73
00:04:25,510 --> 00:04:26,650
How much

74
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,410
do you know about me?

75
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:30,490
About me and Herod, and...

76
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,180
Herod...

77
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,730
Want me to get rid of him for you?

78
00:04:38,290 --> 00:04:41,480
You look like you're about to bolt
over a few words from that bastard.

79
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,480
I can't have that.

80
00:04:42,570 --> 00:04:43,400
What?

81
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:46,770
I'm not interested in
your entanglements with other guys.

82
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:48,440
Focus only on me.

83
00:04:48,810 --> 00:04:50,480
Only on me and my songs.

84
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:55,120
I'll do anything for you.

85
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,630
Really?

86
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:59,520
What I really want is...

87
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,410
Don't follow me.

88
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:18,660
Should I follow him?

89
00:05:19,210 --> 00:05:20,490
Don't blow your cover.

90
00:05:20,770 --> 00:05:23,230
Make sure he gets home safely,
and report back to me.

91
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:24,710
Yes, understood.

92
00:05:43,170 --> 00:05:45,210
Thank you, my errand warrior.

93
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:46,700
I'm back.

94
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,040
Good job.

95
00:05:48,070 --> 00:05:50,070
You're late. Take your punishment.

96
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:51,800
Punishment?

97
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,470
Have a big meal.

98
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,610
I have no appetite.

99
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:59,150
You don't need an appetite.
You eat when it's time.

100
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,100
Eat well, and your mind
will stop wandering.

101
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,570
Go wash your hands now.

102
00:06:02,970 --> 00:06:04,170
Yes.

103
00:06:44,450 --> 00:06:45,510
Are you going to run away?

104
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:46,710
Are you running away?

105
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,690
My dear protégé.

106
00:06:50,970 --> 00:06:52,900
The food is getting cold. Hurry up.

107
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,610
Here, eat this.

108
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,340
Have some of this too.

109
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:05,020
And some dried shredded squid.

110
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,800
Eat more anchovies.

111
00:07:06,810 --> 00:07:09,120
The calcium is good for your bones. Here.

112
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:18,300
How is it? Is it good?

113
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:23,570
That's right. Okay.

114
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,880
[Entertainment Agencies Suspected of
Receiving Mob Funds]

115
00:07:26,730 --> 00:07:29,760
Allegations have emerged that some
prominent entertainment agencies

116
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:32,950
have been operating with funding
from organized crime groups.

117
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:36,900
[Entertainment Agencies Suspected of
Receiving Mob Funds]

118
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:36,740
The police have launched an investigation
after uncovering evidence

119
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:39,770
of the mob's active involvement—
exerting pressure

120
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:43,670
regarding artist contracts
and investment recoupment.

121
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:49,460
Right, watching the news while eating
gives me indigestion.

122
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:53,150
Right. Try the kimchi too.

123
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,850
This batch is loaded with probiotics.

124
00:07:56,909 --> 00:07:58,170
It was well fermented.

125
00:07:58,190 --> 00:07:59,980
-Have a quail egg.
-Okay.

126
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:02,490
Here, get it. Good.

127
00:08:03,670 --> 00:08:05,330
My rice is completely buried.

128
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,390
Eat more.

129
00:08:07,510 --> 00:08:10,760
Fuel up. Tomorrow will be an eventful day.

130
00:08:15,770 --> 00:08:19,610
[Whistleblower Exposes Alleged Ties Between
Entertainment Agency & Criminal Syndicate]

131
00:08:25,170 --> 00:08:26,200
Damn it!

132
00:08:30,170 --> 00:08:31,420
I'm sorry.

133
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:33,409
Which rat is it?

134
00:08:33,650 --> 00:08:34,669
We're looking into it.

135
00:08:34,669 --> 00:08:37,090
Looking into it?
You should be stopping it, Won!

136
00:08:37,090 --> 00:08:39,929
Do you think I sent you there
to make music?

137
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,210
I'm sorry.

138
00:08:46,730 --> 00:08:47,800
Won.

139
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:49,640
Yes.

140
00:08:50,890 --> 00:08:52,410
Anything new these days?

141
00:08:53,470 --> 00:08:54,440
No.

142
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:58,790
You'd better not be
hiding anything from me.

143
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:02,580
We're done here.

144
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:16,270
[Sandol Village]

145
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:16,390
-Here, have the big one.
-Okay, okay.

146
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:19,330
[Special Celebratory Performance
by a Popular Singer From Seoul]

147
00:09:16,670 --> 00:09:17,540
I want one more.

148
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,570
One is a bit stingy, don't you think?

149
00:09:19,570 --> 00:09:20,630
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

150
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,570
-Cheers!
-Cheers. Cheers.

151
00:09:23,110 --> 00:09:25,790
Gosh, Mr. Pan, why are you so late?

152
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:28,650
Mr. Pan, didn't you say
we were going for a walk?

153
00:09:28,650 --> 00:09:29,580
How did we get here?

154
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:31,630
We walked here, didn't we?

155
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,580
This is a disaster!

156
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:36,210
Sandol Village really can't do without me.

157
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:38,030
What's wrong now, Chief?

158
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:40,320
The microphone is screeching,

159
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:42,190
and the singer hasn't shown up.

160
00:09:42,310 --> 00:09:43,990
Maybe the mic is heartbroken.

161
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,650
Why hasn't the singer arrived?

162
00:09:45,650 --> 00:09:47,510
They said they took the wrong way.

163
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:50,710
They went to Sandeul Village
instead of Sandol Village.

164
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,200
It happens.

165
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:54,280
-This is troublesome. What should we do?
-Exactly.

166
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,050
Sit first. Sit.

167
00:09:55,050 --> 00:09:55,900
Sit down.

168
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,130
Take a seat.

169
00:09:59,850 --> 00:10:00,680
Alright.

170
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:02,540
Hello.

171
00:10:05,510 --> 00:10:06,770
I'm good. Thank you.

172
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:09,830
No, thank you. Really.

173
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,030
Just eat it.

174
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:16,870
In Sandol Village, refusing three times
is considered rebellion.

175
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:18,910
Thank you.

176
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:26,550
Okay, everyone!

177
00:10:26,690 --> 00:10:27,640
Everyone!

178
00:10:27,970 --> 00:10:29,570
The singer is here!

179
00:10:29,650 --> 00:10:31,090
-The singer? Where?
-Where?

180
00:10:31,090 --> 00:10:32,030
-Where?
-Where?

181
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:32,830
Here!

182
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,630
Here?

183
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:35,820
-Me?
-Yeah.

184
00:10:35,950 --> 00:10:37,680
I didn't say I was going to sing.

185
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:39,690
But you're eating the appearance deposit.

186
00:10:39,690 --> 00:10:40,600
Huh?

187
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:43,610
Bravo! Come on!

188
00:10:44,850 --> 00:10:46,490
So that's the singer.

189
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:48,160
-Mr. Pan.
-Please.

190
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,220
Mr. Pan.

191
00:10:49,630 --> 00:10:50,940
Please get on stage.

192
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:54,810
Mr. Pan!

193
00:10:57,940 --> 00:10:59,480
Attention, everyone.

194
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:03,710
A round of applause for
our special guest singer!

195
00:11:06,970 --> 00:11:07,990
Hello, everyone.

196
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:10,660
A little introduction:
born and raised in Sandol Village—not,

197
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:14,510
but he just ate our specialty,
Sandol sweet and sour pork.

198
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:16,420
He ate it yesterday, ate it last year,

199
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:17,660
and just ate it again!

200
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:22,580
This is Lee Hanyul, a superstar
shaped by Sandol Village!

201
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:27,130
Music!

202
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:48,110
Dawn always comes softly...

203
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,290
I can't hear you!

204
00:11:51,390 --> 00:11:53,860
Where is his energy?

205
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:55,830
He looks just like my grandson.

206
00:11:57,130 --> 00:11:59,220
You can't make him
sing on an empty stomach!

207
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:01,010
They can't hear well!

208
00:12:01,490 --> 00:12:02,560
Just this once—

209
00:12:02,970 --> 00:12:04,870
if I could...

210
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:11,730
If I could turn back time.

211
00:12:11,850 --> 00:12:13,510
The sound of dawn...

212
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:14,510
That's right!

213
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:17,880
My breath calling out to you.

214
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:26,350
It may fade into the distance,
yet it still reaches toward you.

215
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,910
The sound of dawn...

216
00:13:39,430 --> 00:13:40,470
Young man!

217
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:43,040
Where are you from?
How can you sing so well?

218
00:13:43,070 --> 00:13:44,270
Where are you from?

219
00:13:44,310 --> 00:13:45,640
You have such fair skin.

220
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:46,730
And what a voice!

221
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:49,850
Your singing could melt any woman's heart.

222
00:13:49,990 --> 00:13:52,070
My heart is a puddle right now!

223
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:55,310
Wait...

224
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,560
Thank you.

225
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:59,870
And who is this tall hunk?

226
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,950
He is mine.

227
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:04,000
-Oh my!
-Oh my, oh my!

228
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:06,250
They must be a couple!

229
00:14:06,610 --> 00:14:07,840
It's not like that.

230
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:09,630
I'm a singer under his agency.

231
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:13,450
I had my own season of hot passion, too.

232
00:14:13,630 --> 00:14:16,430
What are you talking about?
It's still not too late for us.

233
00:14:16,430 --> 00:14:17,510
What do you mean?

234
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:19,870
Should I tell my husband
to set the mood tonight?

235
00:14:19,870 --> 00:14:21,070
How? Set what mood?

236
00:14:21,190 --> 00:14:23,320
Get him to do some push-ups to prepare!

237
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:24,650
Like this.

238
00:14:26,930 --> 00:14:28,290
Don't follow me.

239
00:14:29,650 --> 00:14:30,650
He's so handsome.

240
00:14:30,810 --> 00:14:31,520
Oh my god.

241
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:33,070
How can he be so handsome?

242
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:37,970
I just want to go along with him!

243
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:57,900
Hello.

244
00:14:59,030 --> 00:14:59,880
Hello.

245
00:15:00,010 --> 00:15:01,380
I saw you singing.

246
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:02,680
You have a great voice.

247
00:15:02,830 --> 00:15:03,920
Thank you.

248
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:05,530
I was lucky to catch you.

249
00:15:05,830 --> 00:15:08,250
I was just passing by on an errand.

250
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,150
I forgot to introduce myself.

251
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:11,740
I'm...

252
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:15,520
Go Hyunwoo, head of rookie development
at Saebyeok Entertainment.

253
00:15:13,610 --> 00:15:15,400
[Saebyeok Entertainment:
I like your voice. Reach out anytime!]

254
00:15:21,530 --> 00:15:22,840
He is mine.

255
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:24,930
Um,

256
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,320
at least take my card.

257
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:28,280
I said he is mine.

258
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:34,770
Cheers.

259
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:53,800
What are you doing?

260
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,420
I was getting a tissue.

261
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:56,400
What's wrong?

262
00:16:23,950 --> 00:16:25,880
-What?
-I'm going to the restroom.

263
00:16:40,510 --> 00:16:41,860
Don't follow me.

264
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:49,990
I told you not to follow me!

265
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,470
Long time no see.

266
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,260
You were in cahoots with that guy, right?

267
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:12,430
That was aggravated assault.

268
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,560
Attempted murder.

269
00:17:16,270 --> 00:17:17,480
Let go of me.

270
00:17:19,530 --> 00:17:21,790
I guess I should get the police involved.

271
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:25,300
I wonder what will happen to that guy.

272
00:17:32,650 --> 00:17:34,030
Oh, you're still here?

273
00:17:35,370 --> 00:17:36,600
I guessed so.

274
00:17:37,150 --> 00:17:39,350
It's better not make a big deal out of it,

275
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:40,650
right?

276
00:17:45,190 --> 00:17:47,390
You could compensate me with your body.

277
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:51,000
We have to finish
what we started last time.

278
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:58,040
God damn it!

279
00:17:58,050 --> 00:17:59,260
Wow, seriously!

280
00:18:01,110 --> 00:18:02,090
Bring it on!

281
00:18:02,490 --> 00:18:03,640
Lee Won.

282
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,540
I'm sorry about last time.

283
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:16,780
I mistook you for a pervert
and reacted without thinking.

284
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:20,950
Jeez, there goes my chance to throw hands.

285
00:18:20,950 --> 00:18:22,090
Oh, man.

286
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:23,840
Sheesh. Damn it.

287
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:25,670
I knew it.

288
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:27,320
You two really are in cahoots.

289
00:18:27,320 --> 00:18:28,580
Bloody hell.

290
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,830
Give me your number,

291
00:18:32,930 --> 00:18:36,730
and I'll take care of your medical bills
and any other compensation.

292
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:38,170
Tsk.

293
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:45,410
Okay.

294
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:48,180
Now you're talking my language.

295
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:53,570
Make way, won't you?

296
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:55,890
I'll go around you then.

297
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:00,070
Right. Almost forgot.

298
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:06,130
Smile.

299
00:19:09,970 --> 00:19:11,610
Bye, pretty boy.

300
00:19:40,010 --> 00:19:40,820
Lee Won.

301
00:19:41,010 --> 00:19:42,130
Hey!

302
00:19:42,370 --> 00:19:43,900
Where are you going?

303
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:45,040
Lee Won!

304
00:19:57,050 --> 00:19:58,280
I'm so full.

305
00:20:00,210 --> 00:20:02,460
-Mr. Pan.
-Hmm?

306
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:04,970
I have a question.

307
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:06,620
I like questions.

308
00:20:06,710 --> 00:20:07,780
Go ahead.

309
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:11,870
What kind of person is Lee Won?

310
00:20:16,690 --> 00:20:18,530
It's not that.

311
00:20:18,710 --> 00:20:20,730
Since we're working together,

312
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:23,070
I should probably know more about him.

313
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:25,910
That's a relief.

314
00:20:26,310 --> 00:20:27,570
What do you mean?

315
00:20:28,730 --> 00:20:34,090
He's too high maintenance—
not worth the drama.

316
00:20:34,710 --> 00:20:39,130
He must have everything he wants.

317
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:41,380
And the problem is,

318
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:46,850
because of that, he always
crosses the line and creates trouble.

319
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:48,090
That's his problem.

320
00:20:48,670 --> 00:20:51,680
So don't get too close to him,

321
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,160
or you'll get hurt.

322
00:20:56,530 --> 00:20:59,110
Well, it might be too late for you now.

323
00:21:01,290 --> 00:21:02,290
Damn it.

324
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:08,050
Where are the stars?

325
00:21:43,790 --> 00:21:47,590
Why on earth are you doing this?

326
00:21:51,850 --> 00:21:53,110
Look carefully.

327
00:21:57,970 --> 00:21:59,530
Because he is mine.

328
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:02,940
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

329
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,330
This is Adolph's sheet music.

330
00:23:04,330 --> 00:23:05,440
Why is it with you?

331
00:23:05,570 --> 00:23:06,830
I'll give it all to you.

332
00:23:06,850 --> 00:23:07,910
Come with me.

333
00:23:08,150 --> 00:23:09,340
Just you and me.

334
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:10,800
You're telling me

335
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:12,310
you stole Adolph's song

336
00:23:12,650 --> 00:23:13,860
just to trap me?

337
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:15,780
Why did you kill Adolph?

338
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:19,030
I... killed him?

339
00:23:19,310 --> 00:23:20,540
What are you doing?

340
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:25,710
This is the most effective way
to shut me up.
